This case study analyzes the use of Artificial Intelligence in the public sector, focusing on Singapore’s
AI-powered public health system under the Smart Nation initiative. The system uses machine learning, NLP,
and real-time data integration to monitor and predict disease outbreaks, significantly improving response
time and decision-making. 

The study highlights key benefits such as faster outbreak detection, improved predictive accuracy, and
efficient resource allocation. However, it also identifies critical challenges, including data privacy
concerns, algorithmic bias, and the digital divide, which can limit fairness and accessibility.

Additionally, the case study proposes a Real-Time Policy Intelligence Platform, designed to enhance 
policy-making through continuous data analysis, citizen sentiment tracking, and policy simulation.

Overall, the study emphasizes that while AI can transform governance, its success depends on ethical 
implementation, transparency, and strong data governance to ensure responsible and inclusive public 
service delivery.
